                [
                    130.0,
                    322.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "At best, this rule about because reflects a small truth of style. As you will see in Lesson 4, readers prefer sentences to begin with information they know and to proceed to information they don't. But subordinate clauses beginning with because usually convey new information, and so putting one at the beginning of a sentence can be mildly awkward. To begin a sentence with a clause expressing familiar information about causation, use since rather than because, because since implies that the reader already knows what's in the clause:",
            "block_bbox": [
                126,
                334,
                784,
                502
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    126.0,
                    334.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    334.0
                ],
                [
                    784.0,
                    502.0
                ],
                [
                    126.0,
                    502.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Since our language seems to reflect our quality of mind, it is easy for those inclined to look down on others to think that grammatical “errors” indicate mental or moral deficiency.",
            "block_bbox": [
                180,
                515,
                783,
                586
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 7,
            "global_block_id": 7,
            "global_group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    180.0,
                    515.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    515.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    586.0
                ],
                [
                    180.0,
                    586.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "There are exceptions to this principle, but it's generally sound.",
            "block_bbox": [
                129,
                599,
                586,
                623
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    129.0,
                    599.0
                ],
                [
                    586.0,
                    599.0
                ],
                [
                    586.0,
                    623.0
                ],
                [
                    129.0,
                    623.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "“Use the relative pronoun that—not which—for restrictive clauses.”",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                665,
                707,
                721
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 9,
            "global_block_id": 9,
            "global_group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    665.0
                ],
                [
                    707.0,
                    665.0
                ],
                [
                    707.0,
                    721.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    721.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Allegedly not this:",
            "block_bbox": [
                92,
                729,
                254,
                754
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 10,
            "global_block_id": 10,
            "global_group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    92.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    254.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    254.0,
                    754.0
                ],
                [
                    92.0,
                    754.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "✓ Next is a typical situation which a practiced writer corrects “for style” virtually by reflex action.",
            "block_bbox": [
                103,
                767,
                753,
                815
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 11,
            "global_block_id": 11,
            "global_group_id": 11,
            "block_polygon_points": [
