                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Jacques Barzun, Simple and Direct",
            "block_bbox": [
                501,
                830,
                783,
                854
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 12,
            "global_block_id": 12,
            "global_group_id": 12,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    501.0,
                    830.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    830.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    854.0
                ],
                [
                    501.0,
                    854.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Yet just a few sentences before, Barzun himself (one of our most eminent intellectual historians and critics of style) had asserted:",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                867,
                782,
                918
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12,
            "group_id": 13,
            "global_block_id": 13,
            "global_group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    867.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    867.0
                ],
                [
                    782.0,
                    918.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    918.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Us[e] that with defining [i.e., restrictive] clauses except when stylistic reasons interpose.",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                931,
                753,
                956
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 14,
            "global_block_id": 14,
            "global_group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    931.0
                ],
                [
                    753.0,
                    931.0
                ],
                [
                    753.0,
                    956.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    956.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "In that earlier sentence, no such reasons interpose: Barzun's own sense of style simply led him to prefer which.",
            "block_bbox": [
                91,
                969,
                783,
                1019
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 15,
            "global_block_id": 15,
            "global_group_id": 15,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    91.0,
                    969.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    969.0
                ],
                [
                    783.0,
                    1019.0
                ],
                [
                    91.0,
                    1019.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This “rule” is relatively new. It first appeared in 1906 in Henry and Francis Fowler’s The King’s English. The Fowlers thought the random variation between that and which to begin a restrictive clause was messy, so they just asserted that henceforth writers should (with some exceptions) limit which to nonrestrictive clauses. A nonrestrictive clause modifies a noun naming a referent that you can identify unambiguously without the information in that clause. For example:",
            "block_bbox": [
                90,
                1022,
                785,
                1177
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 15,
            "group_id": 16,
            "global_block_id": 16,
            "global_group_id": 16,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    90.0,
                    1022.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    1022.0
                ],
                [
                    785.0,
                    1177.0
                ],
                [
                    90.0,
                    1177.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "✓ The company ended its first bankruptcy, which it had filed in 2012.",
